# External Verification Sources for A014–A017

## Northern cod

1. DFO, *Stock Assessment of Northern Cod (NAFO Divs. 2J3KL) in 2016*, SAR 2016/026: https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/Library/365622.pdf
   - Table A2 verifies the submitted rounded SSB, M, and F values for 1983–2015.
   - The report identifies the values as estimates from the M-shift formulation of NCAM.
   - The report states that 2015 SSB was about 300,000 t and M was 0.28.

2. DFO Northern Cod Framework Proceedings: https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/Library/40687636.pdf
   - The proceedings state that constant-M/wide-catch alternatives fit worse, but caution that in NCAM M refers to unreported deaths and may include de-facto fishing mortality from unreported removals.
   - This prevents identifying estimated M as a directly observed biological cause.

3. DFO 2024 reopening announcement: https://www.canada.ca/en/fisheries-oceans/news/2024/06/the-government-of-canada-announces-the-historic-return-of-the-commercial-northern-cod-fishery-in-newfoundland-and-labrador.html
   - Verifies the 26 June 2024 announcement and Canadian TAC of 18,000 t.

4. Government of Newfoundland and Labrador milestone record: https://www.gov.nl.ca/publicat/tags/text/page34.htm
   - Verifies the 2 July 1992 moratorium announcement.
   - Does not establish a within-year SSB threshold-crossing date.

5. Rose and Walters, *The state of Canada’s iconic Northern cod: A second opinion*: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165783619301614
   - Confirms live structural disagreement over the allocation of mortality to natural mortality and unreported catch.

6. Tam and Bundy 2019 context was checked through later literature summaries, including: https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/faf.70005
   - Confirms the historical capelin benchmark of 13.77 t/km² and continuing debate over capelin/seal/cod mechanisms.
   - Does not independently verify every submitted biomass value or causal discriminant.

## Statistics Canada community measures

7. Statistics Canada, *Statistics on resource-based communities*: https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/pub/16-509-x/2016001/1705-eng.htm
   - Verifies tables 38-10-0167-01 and 38-10-0168-01.
   - Defines fishing-based CSDs through employment-income shares in NAICS aquaculture, fishing, and seafood preparation/packaging.
   - Defines resource-based communities as the top 2% of Canadian CSDs; fishing thresholds are 25.1% in 2016 and 21.4% in 2021.
   - Shows why these CSD records are not equivalent to a panel of 2J3KL inshore licence holders.

## Poverty-line vintage

8. World Bank, *June 2025 Update to Global Poverty Lines*: https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/factsheet/2025/06/05/june-2025-update-to-global-poverty-lines
   - The current primary international poverty line is $3.00/day in 2021 PPP.
   - It replaced $2.15/day in 2017 PPP in June 2025.
   - Historical 2017-PPP estimates remain available in PIP, so $2.15 may be used only with an explicit historical-vintage lock.

## Computational check

9. A014 appendix code was executed in the workspace with SciPy `solve_ivp`; all four submitted assertions passed. This verifies the selected toy simulations only, not a fit to Northern cod or the constrained-M calculations.
